# Model Alignment Rule

Model/provider routing is **DB-first**: pipeline role assignments live in the **admin Registry** (Postgres) and are synced to LiteLLM by reconcile flows. There is no `models.yaml` bootstrap path.

Synesis is Kubernetes-native. OpenShift/OpenShift AI are supported options, not required dependencies.

## When modifying model references:

1. **Update registry-aligned configs** that point at deployed model endpoints:
   - `base/gateway/litellm-config.yaml` — `api_base` for synesis-router, synesis-general, synesis-critic, synesis-coder
   - `base/planner-ts/src/config.ts` — planner model defaults
   - `base/planner-ts/deployment.yaml` — planner-ts runtime env vars
2. **Align Admin Registry expectations** with provider governance defaults and role assignments
3. **Remind the user** to deploy model runtimes (KServe/vLLM/OpenShift AI) and configure endpoints if deployment names differ from defaults (`synesis-router`, `synesis-general`, `synesis-critic`, `synesis-coder`)

## Service URL pattern

`http://<service-name>.<namespace>.svc.cluster.local:8080/v1`

## vLLM config alignment

When router/general/critic/coder fail to start or OOM: check [vLLM Recipes](https://docs.vllm.ai/projects/recipes/en/latest/) and `docs/VLLM_RECIPES.md` for model-specific args (tensor-parallel-size, max-model-len, tool-call-parser, etc.).

## Yarn runtime (separate from vLLM roles)

**Synesis Yarn** (`base/yarn-ts/`) is the OpenAI-compatible IDE/agent runtime; it is **not** a vLLM InferenceService. Model/provider for Yarn come from Yarn env (e.g. `SYNESIS_YARN_PROVIDER`, `SYNESIS_YARN_MODEL`) and/or role-assignment APIs, not from file-based profile definitions. Deployed via `base/yarn-ts` + overlays (`overlays/api`, `overlays/model`), namespace **`synesis-yarn`**.
